1
00:00:10,982 --> 00:00:13,518
<i>The world is full of coincidences.</i>

2
00:00:14,519 --> 00:00:15,787
<i>Twenty-five years ago,</i>

3
00:00:16,888 --> 00:00:18,890
<i>I had a fateful encounter with Mariko.</i>

4
00:00:20,658 --> 00:00:21,493
<i>However…</i>

5
00:00:22,427 --> 00:00:24,229
<i>there are plenty of people</i>

6
00:00:25,263 --> 00:00:27,632
<i>who approach Mariko those who envy her.</i>

7
00:00:28,133 --> 00:00:30,835
<i>I don't want my daughter</i>
<i>to hear about this.</i>

8
00:00:31,402 --> 00:00:33,571
<i>I must do what I need to.</i>

9
00:00:34,072 --> 00:00:37,542
<i>Yukimura is suspected in Tateiwa's case.</i>

10
00:00:40,645 --> 00:00:42,847
It wasn't on camera, was it?

11
00:00:44,249 --> 00:00:46,017
The part where I killed Tateiwa.

12
00:00:47,018 --> 00:00:49,053
<i>Because I'm the one by Mariko's side…</i>

13
00:00:50,255 --> 00:00:51,222
<i>protecting her.</i>

14
00:00:53,791 --> 00:00:56,094
CRIME PREVENTION

15
00:00:56,161 --> 00:00:58,463
TRAFFIC SAFETY

16
00:01:00,698 --> 00:01:02,934
Somebody! Somebody, help!

17
00:01:03,902 --> 00:01:05,770
Somebody! Somebody! Let me go!

18
00:01:06,638 --> 00:01:09,140
Help me! Let me go!

19
00:01:12,677 --> 00:01:14,212
Somebody!

20
00:01:17,182 --> 00:01:19,851
<i>Mariko! I have to save Mariko…</i>

21
00:01:20,418 --> 00:01:21,386
<i>Mariko!</i>

22
00:01:37,235 --> 00:01:40,605
<i>Recently, I've been having</i>
<i>the same dream over and over.</i>

23
00:01:41,539 --> 00:01:44,008
<i>It's a dream about Mariko</i>
<i>almost being kidnapped</i>

24
00:01:44,075 --> 00:01:45,677
<i>25 years ago.</i>

25
00:01:47,912 --> 00:01:50,481
<i>The me in the dream couldn't make a sound,</i>

26
00:01:50,982 --> 00:01:52,717
<i>and I couldn't save Mariko.</i>

27
00:01:54,052 --> 00:01:55,920
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

28
00:01:57,021 --> 00:01:59,390
<i>I couldn't save Mariko in the dream</i>

29
00:02:00,058 --> 00:02:02,927
<i>because I've always just been a bystander.</i>

30
00:02:29,854 --> 00:02:30,788
<i>It's okay.</i>

31
00:02:31,623 --> 00:02:34,158
<i>In reality, seven-year-old me</i>
<i>did protect her.</i>

32
00:02:39,497 --> 00:02:40,632
<i>And it's a new day.</i>

33
00:02:42,634 --> 00:02:48,873
MAIN TITLE

34
00:03:00,151 --> 00:03:01,286
Good morning.

35
00:03:21,806 --> 00:03:26,044
Come on. How is he always there?

36
00:03:26,110 --> 00:03:27,478
Don't scare me like that!

37
00:03:30,248 --> 00:03:31,115
Why?

38
00:03:31,949 --> 00:03:34,686
Why should I be startled? Me?

39
00:03:50,501 --> 00:03:53,671
Manager, Chitose Chemical
delivered the new sample

40
00:03:53,738 --> 00:03:55,840
based on the feedback from last time.

41
00:03:55,907 --> 00:03:57,809
Just leave it there.
I will review it later.

42
00:04:02,513 --> 00:04:05,249
She is in a terrible mood today.

43
00:04:05,316 --> 00:04:07,985
Something bad must have happened.

44
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,241
She flat out…

45
00:04:32,243 --> 00:04:33,678
hates me.

46
00:04:34,312 --> 00:04:37,648
Whenever she sees your face,
she just walks away disgustedly?

47
00:04:41,652 --> 00:04:45,423
I brazenly intervened in Mariko's
personal life. Now she hates me.

48
00:04:46,824 --> 00:04:48,860
What happened, really?

49
00:04:51,496 --> 00:04:53,898
It's to do with her private life.
I can't tell you.

50
00:04:55,933 --> 00:04:56,901
<i>You</i> are saying that?

51
00:04:59,570 --> 00:05:02,039
Tomoya, excuse me, it won't start…

52
00:05:02,106 --> 00:05:04,675
Ah, okay, okay. Time to focus.

53
00:05:05,410 --> 00:05:06,744
Okay, okay, all right.

54
00:05:07,979 --> 00:05:09,947
Ah, I'm starving.

55
00:05:10,014 --> 00:05:12,283
I missed breakfast this morning.

56
00:05:16,154 --> 00:05:19,424
-Izumi, let's go to a different place.
-What, why?

57
00:05:19,490 --> 00:05:20,491
Well, you know,

58
00:05:20,558 --> 00:05:23,027
-it's crowded in here!
-No, it's empty.

59
00:05:23,094 --> 00:05:25,696
-Just come on! Let's go!
-Why?

60
00:05:26,230 --> 00:05:27,565
I was just leaving.

61
00:05:28,166 --> 00:05:29,634
Yukimura…

62
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:31,402
-Tap, please.
-Go ahead.

63
00:05:33,204 --> 00:05:35,807
-Thank you.
-Thank you very much. Excuse me.

64
00:05:45,917 --> 00:05:47,051
Did he leave?

65
00:05:54,492 --> 00:05:56,994
Really, it's nothing.

66
00:06:00,898 --> 00:06:01,799
It's just…

67
00:06:03,034 --> 00:06:06,504
I showed a really pathetic side
of myself to a coworker,

68
00:06:07,605 --> 00:06:09,640
so it's awkward, to say the least.

69
00:06:09,707 --> 00:06:11,175
A pathetic side?

70
00:06:11,242 --> 00:06:13,811
Oh, well, it's no big deal.

71
00:06:15,046 --> 00:06:17,014
I just revealed
too much of my private life.

72
00:06:17,081 --> 00:06:20,818
You don't show your private life
to just anyone, Mariko.

73
00:06:20,885 --> 00:06:25,323
It makes me wonder
who Yukimura really is to you.

74
00:06:25,389 --> 00:06:26,958
You're exaggerating.

75
00:06:27,558 --> 00:06:31,429
-Yukimura's great though, isn't he?
-What?

76
00:06:31,496 --> 00:06:35,833
I mean, are things going well with
that policeman you met at the matchmaking?

77
00:06:36,367 --> 00:06:37,835
Well, it's not…

78
00:06:37,902 --> 00:06:40,004
Mariko, you went to a matchmaking?
You dating anyone?

79
00:06:40,071 --> 00:06:42,206
Aren't you supposed to be working?

80
00:06:42,273 --> 00:06:44,408
It's fine, it's fine.
We barely have any customers.

81
00:06:45,309 --> 00:06:47,278
-Are you sure it's fine?
-Yes, I'm sure.

82
00:06:47,345 --> 00:06:49,480
So, are you dating that matchmaking guy?

83
00:06:49,547 --> 00:06:51,349
No, I'm not dating him.

84
00:06:52,783 --> 00:06:54,619
I see. Thank goodness.

85
00:06:55,386 --> 00:06:56,220
Thank goodness?

86
00:06:58,055 --> 00:06:59,323
Just talking to myself.

87
00:07:00,057 --> 00:07:02,693
Speaking of which,
I've been meaning to ask.

88
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:04,962
Mariko, what's your type?

89
00:07:05,863 --> 00:07:07,465
I've never asked her that either.

90
00:07:10,101 --> 00:07:13,404
I haven't fully analyzed it yet, but…

91
00:07:13,471 --> 00:07:14,772
-Analyzed?
-Analyzed?

92
00:07:15,873 --> 00:07:18,276
…an age range within
five years older or younger.

93
00:07:18,342 --> 00:07:20,811
Living in the central
metropolitan area, male.

94
00:07:20,878 --> 00:07:22,613
Occupation doesn't matter,

95
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:24,682
but it's best if his days off
are the same as mine.

96
00:07:24,749 --> 00:07:28,319
Also, I'm aware that I can be
lacking in communication at times.

97
00:07:28,386 --> 00:07:30,521
While I'll strive to improve on that,

98
00:07:31,055 --> 00:07:33,958
I believe someone talkative, someone

99
00:07:34,025 --> 00:07:36,594
who immediately voices
any questions or doubts, would be ideal.

100
00:07:37,361 --> 00:07:38,195
Yes.

101
00:07:38,930 --> 00:07:40,698
Is that a type?

102
00:07:41,365 --> 00:07:44,101
You sound like you're filling out
a matchmaking requirement sheet.

103
00:07:47,171 --> 00:07:49,974
Why not follow your heart a bit more?

104
00:07:51,909 --> 00:07:52,843
Follow my heart?

105
00:07:54,579 --> 00:07:57,315
When there's a spark in your heart,

106
00:07:57,381 --> 00:07:59,317
you just follow it.

107
00:08:01,619 --> 00:08:05,356
E-Exactly! Well said, Izumi-chan.

108
00:08:05,423 --> 00:08:06,557
Izumi-chan?

109
00:08:06,624 --> 00:08:09,660
I'm quite a bit older than you,
you know? Plus, I've got a kid.

110
00:08:10,628 --> 00:08:13,064
Is this sexual harassment?
Will your husband get mad at me?

111
00:08:30,548 --> 00:08:34,018
By the way, what kind of guys
have you dated in the past?

112
00:08:34,085 --> 00:08:36,821
Guys who seemed like
they weren't bad people.

113
00:08:36,887 --> 00:08:38,956
No wonder it never lasts.

114
00:08:39,023 --> 00:08:40,925
Some people are just like that…

115
00:08:43,828 --> 00:08:44,862
Hello.

116
00:08:45,563 --> 00:08:46,897
Hello.

117
00:08:52,737 --> 00:08:53,804
Oh, Manager…

118
00:08:54,905 --> 00:08:57,108
-Hello.
-Hey there.

119
00:08:57,642 --> 00:08:59,977
Perfect timing, Mariko.
Are you free tonight?

120
00:09:00,044 --> 00:09:01,512
Yes, I am.

121
00:09:01,579 --> 00:09:04,315
I'm meeting with a professor
from Hokuo University. You're joining us.

122
00:09:04,382 --> 00:09:06,217
-Understood.
-Seto, what time?

123
00:09:06,283 --> 00:09:07,652
7:30 p.m.

124
00:09:07,718 --> 00:09:10,921
I'll send you the details shortly.

125
00:09:10,988 --> 00:09:12,556
-All right.
-What about Asai?

126
00:09:14,458 --> 00:09:15,826
He's taking some time off.

127
00:09:17,028 --> 00:09:19,497
Seto will be covering my schedule for now,

128
00:09:19,563 --> 00:09:20,731
so contact him if anything comes up.

129
00:09:21,332 --> 00:09:22,233
For a while?

130
00:09:28,072 --> 00:09:30,174
Did something happen to Asai?

131
00:09:30,708 --> 00:09:32,143
Is he sick or something?

132
00:09:33,110 --> 00:09:34,011
I wonder…

133
00:09:48,726 --> 00:09:50,127
Hey, somebody!

134
00:09:52,563 --> 00:09:54,632
Hey, is anybody there?

135
00:09:56,634 --> 00:09:59,303
I GOT EVERYONE A LOT OF SWEETS
EAT UP! ASAI

136
00:10:08,112 --> 00:10:12,016
<i>There are lots of things in this world</i>
<i>you don't need to know about.</i>

137
00:10:15,820 --> 00:10:20,391
<i>But those who have opened the door,</i>
<i>can't go back.</i>

138
00:10:35,706 --> 00:10:39,744
SECRETARY'S OFFICE

139
00:10:48,352 --> 00:10:49,487
<i>Mariko.</i>

140
00:10:50,121 --> 00:10:52,389
<i>In order to protect you,</i>

141
00:10:52,456 --> 00:10:54,225
<i>I'm doing some pretty questionable things.</i>

142
00:10:55,659 --> 00:10:58,362
<i>If I'm caught,</i>
<i>I can't talk my way out of this.</i>

143
00:10:59,363 --> 00:11:00,931
<i>I may get fired</i>

144
00:11:01,565 --> 00:11:05,469
<i>or even end up in prison…</i>

145
00:11:10,574 --> 00:11:11,942
NOSE

146
00:11:12,009 --> 00:11:14,578
NOSE COSMETICS, LTD.

147
00:11:20,117 --> 00:11:22,086
SERIAL CHILD KIDNAPPER

148
00:11:25,823 --> 00:11:27,258
<i>It was here after all.</i>

149
00:11:28,459 --> 00:11:30,394
<i>The article from 25 years ago.</i>

150
00:11:30,895 --> 00:11:33,164
<i>An article I've never seen,</i>
<i>one not even in my possession.</i>

151
00:11:33,664 --> 00:11:34,498
CONTRADICTS POLICE STATEMENT

152
00:11:34,565 --> 00:11:37,234
<i>Is Asai Mariko's enemy?</i>

153
00:11:37,301 --> 00:11:38,669
<i>Or her ally?</i>

154
00:11:38,736 --> 00:11:39,770
CONNECTION WITH FATHER LEAVES DOUBT
WAS THE KIDNAPPING TRULY RANDOM?

155
00:11:48,746 --> 00:11:51,248
<i>I just need to get Asai</i>

156
00:11:51,982 --> 00:11:53,951
<i>to share his secret with me.</i>

157
00:11:54,451 --> 00:11:55,853
<i>That's all.</i>

158
00:11:56,787 --> 00:11:58,022
<i>That's all I need…</i>

159
00:12:07,031 --> 00:12:08,933
<i>Don't scare me!</i>

160
00:12:08,999 --> 00:12:12,436
<i>Those big eyes, suddenly staring at me,</i>
<i>scare me more than anything else.</i>

161
00:12:22,780 --> 00:12:25,616
<i>My mother used to tell me</i>

162
00:12:27,484 --> 00:12:32,356
<i>that I only looked at what's in front</i>
<i>of me and never thought about the future.</i>

163
00:12:33,724 --> 00:12:35,259
<i>"I'm sorry, Mom."</i>

164
00:12:35,759 --> 00:12:38,929
<i>They say you can't teach</i>
<i>an old dog new tricks.</i>

165
00:12:38,996 --> 00:12:40,097
<i>And it's true.</i>

166
00:12:41,432 --> 00:12:45,169
<i>Even if I die and go to hell someday,</i>

167
00:12:46,437 --> 00:12:48,806
<i>as long as I can avoid</i>
<i>going to prison right now,</i>

168
00:12:49,707 --> 00:12:50,808
<i>that's enough.</i>

169
00:12:53,077 --> 00:12:54,345
GINJIRO NOSE

170
00:12:58,682 --> 00:13:00,050
GINJIRO NOSE

171
00:13:00,117 --> 00:13:00,751
INCORRECT PASSWORD

172
00:13:02,519 --> 00:13:03,621
INCORRECT PASSWORD

173
00:13:05,122 --> 00:13:08,392
<i>There must be 50,000 combinations…</i>

174
00:13:12,263 --> 00:13:13,497
KEIMEI UNIVERSITY, CLASS OF 1989

175
00:13:13,564 --> 00:13:14,732
TO THE FRIENDS AT THE UNIVERSITY
ROWING CLUB, REUNITING AFTER 30 YEARS

176
00:13:28,646 --> 00:13:29,980
HUMAN RESOURCES - BUSINESS RELATIONS

177
00:13:30,047 --> 00:13:31,248
INTERNAL ESTIMATES

178
00:13:33,417 --> 00:13:34,551
EMAIL

179
00:13:39,723 --> 00:13:40,524
GOTO ASAI

180
00:13:40,591 --> 00:13:42,092
GOOD MORNING, THIS IS ASAI

181
00:13:42,159 --> 00:13:44,061
DUE TO MY MOTHER'S POOR HEALTH

182
00:13:44,128 --> 00:13:45,696
I WILL BE TAKING AN EXTENDED LEAVE

183
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:25,602
Sorry about that.
Thanks for watching the room.

184
00:14:25,669 --> 00:14:27,204
No problem at all.

185
00:14:27,271 --> 00:14:29,173
The front alarm was malfunctioning.

186
00:14:29,773 --> 00:14:31,342
Didn't seem like
anything was wrong, though.

187
00:14:31,408 --> 00:14:34,011
I see. That's a relief.

188
00:14:34,078 --> 00:14:37,014
Let's eat those snacks you brought us.

189
00:14:37,648 --> 00:14:38,549
Thanks as always.

190
00:14:40,417 --> 00:14:42,152
<i>I was lucky.</i>

191
00:14:43,587 --> 00:14:45,155
<i>Close call.</i>

192
00:14:48,625 --> 00:14:51,328
-Thanks a lot.
-Thank you for the meal.

193
00:14:51,395 --> 00:14:53,230
-I look forward to meeting you again.
-Likewise.

194
00:14:58,802 --> 00:15:01,305
Thank you for tonight.
I'll be taking my leave.

195
00:15:01,372 --> 00:15:04,775
Ride with me. I'll drive you home.

196
00:15:04,842 --> 00:15:07,111
-That's fine. Trains are still running.
-Just come.

197
00:15:17,488 --> 00:15:19,123
<i>I have a bad feeling about this.</i>

198
00:15:20,257 --> 00:15:21,091
<i>And</i>

199
00:15:21,625 --> 00:15:26,230
<i>I hope she forgives me, who, idiotically,</i>
<i>realized this bad feeling too late.</i>

200
00:15:55,959 --> 00:16:00,264
From now on, make sure you never
walk around alone late at night.

201
00:16:02,699 --> 00:16:04,201
Shall I get you a chauffeur?

202
00:16:04,868 --> 00:16:06,003
What?

203
00:16:06,070 --> 00:16:07,638
Remember the Tateiwa case?

204
00:16:08,939 --> 00:16:10,207
Be careful.

205
00:16:12,409 --> 00:16:13,243
Okay…

206
00:16:14,678 --> 00:16:17,114
Oh, but I don't need a chauffeur.

207
00:16:20,717 --> 00:16:21,952
I see…

208
00:16:29,226 --> 00:16:30,060
Um…

209
00:16:32,830 --> 00:16:34,965
I'm sorry about the other day.

210
00:16:37,768 --> 00:16:39,536
Mom's ring…

211
00:16:40,370 --> 00:16:42,739
I know Sayuri had it fixed

212
00:16:43,273 --> 00:16:45,342
out of good intentions.

213
00:16:46,944 --> 00:16:48,445
Tell her I said thank you.

214
00:17:02,860 --> 00:17:04,928
A CONTRADICTION IN THE POLICE REPORT

215
00:17:04,995 --> 00:17:06,730
<i>A contradiction in the police report.</i>

216
00:17:08,332 --> 00:17:12,402
<i>Why didn't the police make this fact</i>
<i>public in the first place?</i>

217
00:17:13,704 --> 00:17:15,372
<i>Did the president cover it up?</i>

218
00:17:15,439 --> 00:17:17,174
TORU URAHARA - CROSSLINE PUBLISHING

219
00:17:22,646 --> 00:17:24,581
CROSSLINE PUBLISHING

220
00:17:25,816 --> 00:17:27,751
TORU URAHARA - CROSSLINE PUBLISHING

221
00:17:32,055 --> 00:17:34,591
GOOD MORNING, THIS IS ASAI

222
00:17:35,259 --> 00:17:36,927
SATORU HATANO

223
00:17:39,730 --> 00:17:43,767
<i>Was Asai investigating</i>
<i>something about Hatano?</i>

224
00:17:43,834 --> 00:17:45,202
SATORU HATANO

225
00:17:45,269 --> 00:17:46,737
EXCLUSIVE INTERVIEW - SHOCKING!

226
00:18:10,694 --> 00:18:13,830
I wondered who was snooping around me.

227
00:18:14,898 --> 00:18:17,901
And it turned out to be
the President's henchman.

228
00:18:18,802 --> 00:18:21,705
-Were you told to keep tabs on me?
-No!

229
00:18:21,772 --> 00:18:23,440
The President knows nothing.

230
00:18:23,507 --> 00:18:25,642
-I was acting on my own.
-On your own?

231
00:18:26,276 --> 00:18:27,110
What?

232
00:18:27,644 --> 00:18:31,081
Acting on righteous fury?
What were you planning to do?

233
00:18:34,818 --> 00:18:36,119
Hey!

234
00:18:38,222 --> 00:18:41,692
You told the weekly mags
all sorts of stuff, right?

235
00:18:42,859 --> 00:18:43,927
So?

236
00:18:45,462 --> 00:18:47,264
You wanted to keep me quiet, huh?

237
00:18:49,766 --> 00:18:50,867
Let me out of here.

238
00:18:51,435 --> 00:18:54,404
I won't tell anyone about this.
Let's pretend this never happened.

239
00:18:55,272 --> 00:18:56,707
Hey, I'm begging you!

240
00:18:56,773 --> 00:18:59,176
You were caught once
and suffered for it, right?

241
00:18:59,876 --> 00:19:01,678
Don't commit more crimes!

242
00:19:01,745 --> 00:19:04,481
I was in prison for 25 years.

243
00:19:05,315 --> 00:19:08,385
I want to return the favor.

244
00:19:09,286 --> 00:19:10,120
What on earth

245
00:19:11,054 --> 00:19:12,723
did the President ever do to you?

246
00:19:14,691 --> 00:19:16,560
Let's see.

247
00:19:17,961 --> 00:19:19,730
He did nothing.

248
00:19:20,897 --> 00:19:25,502
He's done nothing, yet he gets
an easy life because his family is rich.

249
00:19:26,036 --> 00:19:27,571
How is that fair?

250
00:19:30,307 --> 00:19:33,877
Ever since we were kids,
I couldn't stand him.

251
00:19:38,081 --> 00:19:40,784
What are you planning to do? Huh?

252
00:19:40,851 --> 00:19:43,387
Is it money? If he gives you
money, you'll be satis--

253
00:19:44,221 --> 00:19:47,758
Well, I wouldn't say no to money.

254
00:19:48,558 --> 00:19:49,459
But

255
00:19:50,260 --> 00:19:53,797
there is something else
that will quell my anger better.

256
00:19:56,833 --> 00:19:59,403
What do you think it is? Huh?

257
00:20:09,179 --> 00:20:12,683
The ratio of carbomer solution
and dimethicone is still high.

258
00:20:12,749 --> 00:20:15,819
It won't create the heavy texture we want.

259
00:20:17,421 --> 00:20:20,557
Let's refine the concept brief a bit more
and resend it to the supplier.

260
00:20:20,624 --> 00:20:21,558
Okay.

261
00:20:21,625 --> 00:20:25,062
Is "high luxury" too vague
of an expression in the first place?

262
00:20:25,595 --> 00:20:27,964
Or am I being too greedy?

263
00:20:28,031 --> 00:20:30,334
Do I have to give up something?

264
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:38,442
-What?
-Oh, uh,

265
00:20:39,042 --> 00:20:39,943
sorry.

266
00:20:44,748 --> 00:20:47,551
Please forget about what happened
on my birthday.

267
00:20:48,385 --> 00:20:49,486
<i>Something was wrong with me.</i>

268
00:20:51,888 --> 00:20:53,924
I don't remember anything.

269
00:20:57,027 --> 00:20:58,762
Good then.

270
00:21:03,934 --> 00:21:07,738
Yesterday, I actually had
a normal conversation with my father.

271
00:21:08,638 --> 00:21:12,843
He's right. It's useless
to keep acting stubborn at my age.

272
00:21:15,445 --> 00:21:17,180
You really are kind, Mariko.

273
00:21:18,682 --> 00:21:20,350
I think you're the only one
who thinks that.

274
00:21:20,417 --> 00:21:22,419
If so, everyone else must be blind.

275
00:21:29,326 --> 00:21:30,861
All right then, handle the brief.

276
00:21:30,927 --> 00:21:33,163
-Understood.
-Thank you.

277
00:21:54,050 --> 00:21:55,085
So?

278
00:21:55,152 --> 00:21:59,189
Since when have you
liked Mariko, Yukimura?

279
00:21:59,756 --> 00:22:00,624
What?

280
00:22:01,291 --> 00:22:03,727
-I don't--
-You're so easy to read.

281
00:22:05,162 --> 00:22:07,664
I don't think Mariko has realized it yet.

282
00:22:08,198 --> 00:22:11,601
She's quite dense.

283
00:22:15,071 --> 00:22:17,908
If you don't say it out loud,

284
00:22:18,442 --> 00:22:20,577
I think she'll go
her entire life without knowing.

285
00:22:42,799 --> 00:22:45,302
PRIVATE INVESTIGATOR

286
00:22:45,969 --> 00:22:47,270
I'm sorry,

287
00:22:47,337 --> 00:22:50,607
but it'd be a breach of confidentiality
to give you client information.

288
00:22:50,674 --> 00:22:53,310
But Tateiwa was telling me about it

289
00:22:53,376 --> 00:22:56,913
before he passed away.

290
00:22:56,980 --> 00:22:59,983
He said if anything happened to him,
I must come here for information.

291
00:23:01,751 --> 00:23:03,987
I mean, if he hadn't told me that,

292
00:23:04,054 --> 00:23:07,657
then how would I know to come here?

293
00:23:08,992 --> 00:23:10,193
Excuse me for asking,

294
00:23:10,961 --> 00:23:13,230
but what was your relationship
with Tateiwa?

295
00:23:13,930 --> 00:23:15,465
If I tell you,
will you give me information?

296
00:23:16,299 --> 00:23:18,001
I can't. No way.

297
00:23:18,068 --> 00:23:19,269
Sorry.

298
00:23:32,449 --> 00:23:34,684
No! I can't.

299
00:23:34,751 --> 00:23:39,623
This is just my gratitude
for our meeting today.

300
00:23:40,457 --> 00:23:41,758
Nothing else.

301
00:23:47,230 --> 00:23:48,265
What?

302
00:23:52,302 --> 00:23:54,671
I meant to make a phone call.

303
00:23:54,738 --> 00:23:57,073
That's right. Excuse me for a moment.

304
00:23:57,574 --> 00:23:59,509
Let's see…

305
00:24:01,811 --> 00:24:03,446
Excuse me for a moment.

306
00:24:04,915 --> 00:24:07,918
Ah, hello? It's me, it's me.

307
00:24:11,655 --> 00:24:13,256
‎INVESTIGATION REPORT

308
00:24:18,628 --> 00:24:19,696
<i>A love motel room?</i>

309
00:24:19,763 --> 00:24:21,364
Definitely.

310
00:24:22,532 --> 00:24:24,334
I got a call from his wife this afternoon.

311
00:24:24,401 --> 00:24:25,969
She was putting his affairs in order,

312
00:24:26,036 --> 00:24:29,306
and it turns out Tateiwa was renting
a room his family knew nothing about.

313
00:24:30,507 --> 00:24:33,376
It was a plain, ordinary room, but…

314
00:24:33,443 --> 00:24:36,212
It's got to do with his womanizing.

315
00:24:36,947 --> 00:24:40,483
-Did anything turn up in the room?
-No, nothing.

316
00:24:40,550 --> 00:24:42,652
It was unnaturally empty.

317
00:24:42,719 --> 00:24:45,655
There was no data left
on his laptop either.

318
00:24:47,591 --> 00:24:51,928
Did someone who knew about
this room's existence take everything?

319
00:24:52,963 --> 00:24:54,297
I would say his mistress.

320
00:24:59,269 --> 00:25:03,440
According to the autopsy results,
among the three stab wounds,

321
00:25:03,506 --> 00:25:06,309
the one that became the fatal blow
is this chest wound, right?

322
00:25:07,577 --> 00:25:09,412
-Yes.
-And

323
00:25:09,479 --> 00:25:15,485
that fatal chest wound
was likely the very first strike.

324
00:25:17,187 --> 00:25:21,491
Reaching the heart from between
the ribs in the left chest…

325
00:25:22,592 --> 00:25:25,629
To inflict a wound of that depth…

326
00:25:27,297 --> 00:25:28,965
So does that mean the suspect is a man?

327
00:25:29,766 --> 00:25:31,968
Wouldn't you say
that's a strong possibility?

328
00:25:32,502 --> 00:25:34,771
In the end, the most suspicious one

329
00:25:35,305 --> 00:25:37,907
is that man caught on the security camera

330
00:25:38,475 --> 00:25:39,509
near the crime scene.

331
00:25:41,745 --> 00:25:43,546
Sota Yukimura.

332
00:25:47,651 --> 00:25:49,686
But the murder weapon hasn't been found,

333
00:25:49,753 --> 00:25:52,255
and the motive isn't really clear.

334
00:25:52,322 --> 00:25:53,356
SOTA YUKIMURA

335
00:26:02,532 --> 00:26:03,500
Here you go.

336
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:05,235
Thank you.

337
00:26:07,003 --> 00:26:07,871
Enjoy.

338
00:26:12,275 --> 00:26:14,010
Apologies for bothering you at work.

339
00:26:14,544 --> 00:26:15,445
It's okay.

340
00:26:17,781 --> 00:26:19,215
It's a lovely cafe.

341
00:26:19,883 --> 00:26:21,251
Do you come here often?

342
00:26:21,785 --> 00:26:25,388
Yes, it's close to the company,
and I like the atmosphere.

343
00:26:29,059 --> 00:26:30,927
It's not good to mix business
with private affairs,

344
00:26:31,461 --> 00:26:33,997
so let me state this up front.

345
00:26:35,265 --> 00:26:38,068
Today, we'll talk about work.

346
00:26:39,602 --> 00:26:40,603
Okay.

347
00:26:40,670 --> 00:26:42,439
I heard Souta Yukimura

348
00:26:43,006 --> 00:26:46,609
was transferred to your department
very recently.

349
00:26:48,344 --> 00:26:49,212
Yes.

350
00:26:49,879 --> 00:26:51,214
Is there an issue with that?

351
00:26:51,281 --> 00:26:52,816
It's nothing big.

352
00:26:53,383 --> 00:26:54,217
I just heard

353
00:26:55,118 --> 00:26:57,220
you selected him.

354
00:27:00,623 --> 00:27:04,060
Were you close prior to that?

355
00:27:05,462 --> 00:27:06,296
No.

356
00:27:06,996 --> 00:27:09,899
Even though we're at the same company,
we had no interaction,

357
00:27:10,433 --> 00:27:12,035
so I didn't know him at all.

358
00:27:13,236 --> 00:27:14,871
Then why him?

359
00:27:16,840 --> 00:27:20,543
One time, we had a brief chance to talk,

360
00:27:20,610 --> 00:27:23,446
and I thought he was very capable.

361
00:27:24,013 --> 00:27:24,848
I see.

362
00:27:26,816 --> 00:27:30,019
What's Yukimura usually like?

363
00:27:32,055 --> 00:27:33,056
Um,

364
00:27:33,723 --> 00:27:36,559
does this have to do with the case?

365
00:27:37,594 --> 00:27:38,495
I'm sorry.

366
00:27:39,095 --> 00:27:41,531
-We're investigating from all angles.
-So,

367
00:27:41,598 --> 00:27:43,133
you really do suspect Yukimura?

368
00:27:47,403 --> 00:27:48,705
I'm sorry.

369
00:27:48,772 --> 00:27:50,273
You can't answer that, right?

370
00:27:51,407 --> 00:27:52,308
No.

371
00:27:52,909 --> 00:27:55,145
I've never been involved
with a criminal case before.

372
00:27:56,079 --> 00:27:58,381
I mean, it's not exactly normal.

373
00:27:59,783 --> 00:28:02,786
So, honestly, I still can't believe it.

374
00:28:03,853 --> 00:28:04,954
Yes.

375
00:28:06,055 --> 00:28:06,956
But

376
00:28:08,391 --> 00:28:10,727
I really think Yukimura is different.

377
00:28:12,562 --> 00:28:14,430
He's… How do I put it?

378
00:28:15,331 --> 00:28:19,068
He's someone who always worries
about others rather than himself.

379
00:28:19,669 --> 00:28:21,638
Someone who seems like
he couldn't even kill a bug.

380
00:28:22,705 --> 00:28:25,375
He probably came under suspicion

381
00:28:25,441 --> 00:28:27,410
because of my relationship with Tateiwa,

382
00:28:27,477 --> 00:28:29,112
but he really is innocent.

383
00:28:33,917 --> 00:28:37,220
I understand what you're saying.

384
00:28:45,595 --> 00:28:46,596
Mariko.

385
00:28:47,397 --> 00:28:49,098
Here you go.

386
00:28:50,533 --> 00:28:51,968
Thank you very much.

387
00:28:53,102 --> 00:28:54,604
Was that the matchmaking guy?

388
00:28:56,539 --> 00:29:00,176
So he was! Are you going to date him?

389
00:29:01,778 --> 00:29:03,947
I think he seems like a nice person, but…

390
00:29:07,917 --> 00:29:10,687
Don't you feel like you and I are similar?

391
00:29:12,188 --> 00:29:14,023
I've never felt
a spark with anyone either.

392
00:29:16,092 --> 00:29:18,795
What were you like
back in your student days?

393
00:29:18,862 --> 00:29:20,263
Any bittersweet memories?

394
00:29:21,798 --> 00:29:23,700
Even I have that much…

395
00:29:25,468 --> 00:29:26,870
In middle school,

396
00:29:27,637 --> 00:29:29,305
<i>I was asked on a date</i>
<i>to a summer festival.</i>

397
00:29:30,874 --> 00:29:33,343
<i>It was my first time going out with a boy,</i>

398
00:29:33,409 --> 00:29:36,412
<i>so I was nervous</i>
<i>and couldn't talk much at all.</i>

399
00:29:37,280 --> 00:29:39,849
Cute. Classic story.

400
00:29:40,617 --> 00:29:41,584
But

401
00:29:41,651 --> 00:29:45,788
to him, it probably looked like
I wasn't having any fun at all.

402
00:29:47,657 --> 00:29:49,859
So he left halfway through and went home.

403
00:29:50,393 --> 00:29:51,294
What? He left you?

404
00:29:52,128 --> 00:29:54,831
-I guess…
-Wow, that guy sucks.

405
00:29:54,898 --> 00:29:57,233
No, it was 100% my fault.

406
00:29:57,300 --> 00:29:59,669
I was expressionless.
You couldn't tell what I was thinking.

407
00:29:59,736 --> 00:30:01,404
He must be scared.

408
00:30:02,572 --> 00:30:03,506
So you are aware of it.

409
00:30:04,841 --> 00:30:05,708
I guess so.

410
00:30:05,775 --> 00:30:07,911
But did you feel a spark with that boy?

411
00:30:08,845 --> 00:30:11,581
No, I didn't.

412
00:30:11,648 --> 00:30:13,683
The heck, so you never had anyone!

413
00:30:15,785 --> 00:30:18,221
Well, forget it! Enough about me.

414
00:30:24,794 --> 00:30:27,830
I envy it, you know.

415
00:30:30,033 --> 00:30:31,668
It doesn't matter if it works out or not.

416
00:30:31,734 --> 00:30:34,003
It's incredible just to have someone.

417
00:30:36,239 --> 00:30:39,175
That guy too,
he's liked the same girl for a long time.

418
00:30:40,343 --> 00:30:43,446
How someone can keep thinking
of one person for so many years

419
00:30:43,513 --> 00:30:45,348
is a mystery to me.

420
00:30:47,250 --> 00:30:48,952
That's just the kind of guy Sota is.

421
00:31:06,836 --> 00:31:08,404
-Hello.
-Hello.

422
00:31:18,247 --> 00:31:19,248
Here you go.

423
00:31:20,416 --> 00:31:21,250
It's fine.

424
00:31:21,918 --> 00:31:24,887
You don't need to do that.
It's not part of your job.

425
00:31:26,356 --> 00:31:27,323
I'm sorry.

426
00:31:38,334 --> 00:31:40,970
She didn't need to say it so harshly.

427
00:31:42,105 --> 00:31:45,675
But honestly, I thought
it was a bit calculated too.

428
00:31:47,176 --> 00:31:50,179
Serving coffee to get liked
by the boss, you know?

429
00:31:51,514 --> 00:31:54,417
That's not what I was trying to do.

430
00:31:54,484 --> 00:31:59,055
Mariko seriously hates
being given special treatment like that.

431
00:32:02,058 --> 00:32:02,892
<i>Mariko.</i>

432
00:32:04,060 --> 00:32:07,730
<i>Have you been thinking of me</i>
<i>as a calculating person,</i>

433
00:32:07,797 --> 00:32:11,234
<i>trying to win favor</i>
<i>with the boss, ever since then?</i>

434
00:32:16,973 --> 00:32:20,343
-Good work today, everyone. Goodbye.
-Bye.

435
00:32:23,980 --> 00:32:26,482
<i>Was I wrong all along?</i>

436
00:32:43,166 --> 00:32:47,136
<i>Even if Mariko is starting to hate me,</i>

437
00:32:48,738 --> 00:32:50,840
<i>there are still things I must do.</i>

438
00:33:01,584 --> 00:33:03,352
Did I say something I shouldn't have?

439
00:33:04,620 --> 00:33:05,521
What was that?

440
00:33:05,588 --> 00:33:07,557
Oh, nothing.

441
00:33:07,623 --> 00:33:10,426
You certainly do need a man
to help with this, huh?

442
00:33:10,493 --> 00:33:11,394
-Right?
-Yes.

443
00:33:11,461 --> 00:33:13,563
Delivery fees are so high!

444
00:33:13,629 --> 00:33:16,933
-I ran into you at the perfect time.
-No problem.

445
00:33:16,999 --> 00:33:20,236
Kinda feels like a park date, right?

446
00:33:20,837 --> 00:33:24,707
-It's exciting, like we're school kids.
-Sara! We're going home!

447
00:33:24,774 --> 00:33:27,410
What? I don't want to go home yet!

448
00:33:27,477 --> 00:33:30,213
What? I don't want to go home yet!

449
00:33:30,279 --> 00:33:32,582
Hey, that's enough.

450
00:33:32,648 --> 00:33:35,151
-I've got to make dinner.
-Cheapskate!

451
00:33:36,986 --> 00:33:40,389
Okay, if you can take the ball
from me now, you win.

452
00:33:40,456 --> 00:33:42,091
Okay, let's go.

453
00:33:47,296 --> 00:33:48,331
Got it?

454
00:33:49,765 --> 00:33:50,633
Can you reach it?

455
00:33:54,770 --> 00:33:56,072
Not bad.

456
00:34:02,812 --> 00:34:04,714
This was sent to my husband?

457
00:34:04,780 --> 00:34:07,917
Yes. It seems it was sent to him
on the exact day the incident occurred.

458
00:34:08,951 --> 00:34:10,119
Okay.

459
00:34:11,120 --> 00:34:14,457
If you get any more information,
report back to me immediately.

460
00:34:14,524 --> 00:34:15,825
Understood.

461
00:34:36,179 --> 00:34:38,614
TV COMMERCIAL

462
00:34:40,683 --> 00:34:42,018
SHINAGAWA STREET MALE STABBING VICTIM

463
00:34:42,084 --> 00:34:43,252
WAS A NOSE COSMETICS EXECUTIVE!

464
00:34:43,319 --> 00:34:44,754
RUMORS ABOUT THE COMPANY'S SHADY DEALINGS

465
00:34:44,820 --> 00:34:48,157
So people finally found out…

466
00:34:48,224 --> 00:34:50,426
Since major media isn't reporting
the details,

467
00:34:50,493 --> 00:34:52,795
rumors are running wild online

468
00:34:52,862 --> 00:34:54,363
about Nose Cosmetics's shady side.

469
00:34:54,430 --> 00:34:55,498
THE AMBITION OF AN EXECUTIVE

470
00:34:55,565 --> 00:34:58,568
Well, it can't be helped.
The way it all looks…

471
00:34:59,068 --> 00:35:03,072
It sounds like
Mariko will be suspected, right?

472
00:35:10,213 --> 00:35:11,047
Everyone.

473
00:35:15,952 --> 00:35:18,721
I'm changing my schedule today
and going out.

474
00:35:19,455 --> 00:35:22,892
I think the clients
have seen this article too,

475
00:35:22,959 --> 00:35:24,126
so I'll go explain in person.

476
00:35:27,463 --> 00:35:29,966
Um, I'll accompany you.

477
00:35:44,513 --> 00:35:48,117
I'm really sorry about this.

478
00:35:55,992 --> 00:35:58,761
I'm glad everyone was understanding.

479
00:36:03,099 --> 00:36:05,868
Did you follow me, thinking
I was going to get yelled at?

480
00:36:05,935 --> 00:36:06,836
No.

481
00:36:07,503 --> 00:36:08,838
It wasn't like that.

482
00:36:22,785 --> 00:36:24,620
Oh, I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

483
00:36:26,022 --> 00:36:27,290
No, it's fine.

484
00:36:36,599 --> 00:36:39,001
I'm sorry. I'm a bit thirsty.

485
00:36:39,068 --> 00:36:40,169
Can we take a break?

486
00:36:40,736 --> 00:36:42,238
-Oh, sure…
-Sorry.

487
00:37:04,126 --> 00:37:05,761
Which one do you want?

488
00:37:05,828 --> 00:37:07,897
You bought them. You decide.

489
00:37:07,963 --> 00:37:09,131
It's fine.

490
00:37:10,333 --> 00:37:11,334
This one, then.

491
00:37:20,576 --> 00:37:21,444
Also…

492
00:37:22,111 --> 00:37:23,145
Here.

493
00:37:24,380 --> 00:37:25,581
Right there…

494
00:37:27,950 --> 00:37:29,952
What? That's scary. You're too sharp-eyed.

495
00:37:31,520 --> 00:37:33,923
Sorry, that was creepy, right?

496
00:37:35,257 --> 00:37:37,793
No, no, I didn't mean it like that.

497
00:37:39,562 --> 00:37:40,463
Thank you.

498
00:37:51,340 --> 00:37:53,609
-What should we do?
-Hmm, what should we do?

499
00:37:53,676 --> 00:37:55,778
-How about target practice?
-Let's get yakisoba.

500
00:37:55,845 --> 00:37:57,413
-Yes!
-I want yakisoba too.

501
00:37:57,480 --> 00:37:59,014
-Me too!
-Yeah!

502
00:37:59,081 --> 00:38:00,416
I'm starving!

503
00:38:02,752 --> 00:38:04,153
What kind of feeling is it?

504
00:38:07,089 --> 00:38:09,258
You've liked the same person
for a long time, right?

505
00:38:18,167 --> 00:38:20,169
Your friend at the cafe mentioned it.

506
00:38:22,037 --> 00:38:23,038
Tomoya…

507
00:38:25,975 --> 00:38:27,943
What makes you like that person so much?

508
00:38:37,086 --> 00:38:38,754
You probably don't want
to talk about this at work.

509
00:38:38,821 --> 00:38:40,823
I'm sorry, that was impolite.

510
00:38:53,936 --> 00:38:56,906
Her sense of justice, I suppose…

511
00:39:02,445 --> 00:39:07,049
She walks straight down
the path she chose…

512
00:39:09,852 --> 00:39:11,754
and works so hard for it

513
00:39:14,590 --> 00:39:16,659
Even though she stands out so much,

514
00:39:18,661 --> 00:39:22,064
she's not someone who wants to stand out.

515
00:39:27,636 --> 00:39:30,973
When given special treatment,
she makes a sour face…

516
00:39:33,809 --> 00:39:35,945
She's mature, pure-hearted,

517
00:39:37,646 --> 00:39:41,016
and always worrying about stuff.

518
00:39:42,718 --> 00:39:46,922
But she desperately tries
to live without relying on anyone.

519
00:39:49,158 --> 00:39:52,995
She's kind to people, things, everything.

520
00:39:53,963 --> 00:39:55,531
She doesn't lie.

521
00:39:57,032 --> 00:39:59,502
Anyway, she's cool.

522
00:40:08,177 --> 00:40:09,745
She's my hero.

523
00:40:15,417 --> 00:40:18,320
Well, I guess it should be heroine, huh?

524
00:40:23,158 --> 00:40:24,260
Let's go.

525
00:40:29,265 --> 00:40:31,367
I'm sorry. Thank you.

526
00:40:34,837 --> 00:40:35,804
Here.

527
00:40:39,508 --> 00:40:40,709
Sorry.

528
00:40:45,014 --> 00:40:45,881
Here.

529
00:40:46,515 --> 00:40:47,816
I love that character.

530
00:40:47,883 --> 00:40:49,618
KOGEBAN

531
00:40:54,490 --> 00:40:56,659
It was popular back when
I was in middle school.

532
00:40:57,459 --> 00:41:00,162
Once I like something,
I tend to stay attached to it forever.

533
00:41:01,964 --> 00:41:05,234
I still use it. Childish, right?

534
00:41:23,886 --> 00:41:26,188
FESTIVAL

535
00:41:30,392 --> 00:41:33,462
We still have time
until the fireworks. Are you hungry?

536
00:41:33,529 --> 00:41:35,698
-How about some takoyaki?
-Anything's fine.

537
00:41:36,198 --> 00:41:38,000
Hey, Hiroto!

538
00:41:38,567 --> 00:41:40,569
Hiroto, come hang out with us!

539
00:41:40,636 --> 00:41:42,738
Idiot, he's on a date!

540
00:41:42,805 --> 00:41:45,007
-Oh, okay.
-Let's go.

541
00:41:46,141 --> 00:41:47,076
I'm going with them.

542
00:41:48,677 --> 00:41:49,545
Hey!

543
00:41:49,612 --> 00:41:50,579
Hey!

544
00:41:50,646 --> 00:41:52,214
-Let's go!
-What, seriously?

545
00:41:52,281 --> 00:41:53,649
-It's fine, it's fine, let's go!
-What?

546
00:42:04,226 --> 00:42:05,127
Sorry!

547
00:42:08,497 --> 00:42:11,433
FESTIVAL

548
00:42:45,968 --> 00:42:47,403
<i>August 8th.</i>

549
00:42:48,504 --> 00:42:50,172
<i>Today was the summer festival.</i>

550
00:42:51,974 --> 00:42:55,577
<i>Mariko was asked out</i>
<i>on a date by a boy in our class.</i>

551
00:42:57,680 --> 00:42:58,681
<i>To be honest,</i>

552
00:42:59,448 --> 00:43:01,150
<i>my chest felt tight.</i>

553
00:43:02,818 --> 00:43:05,254
<i>Even though I decided to watch over her</i>

554
00:43:06,321 --> 00:43:08,857
<i>and thought that I just</i>
<i>wanted her to be happy…</i>

555
00:43:11,160 --> 00:43:13,295
<i>If he can't see Mariko's charm,</i>

556
00:43:13,862 --> 00:43:14,997
<i>he's got no sense at all.</i>

557
00:43:17,099 --> 00:43:20,135
<i>Mariko, I don't want you to get hurt…</i>

558
00:43:30,079 --> 00:43:30,979
Sakura!

559
00:43:31,046 --> 00:43:31,980
Sakura!

560
00:43:33,415 --> 00:43:34,983
We found DNA from someone

561
00:43:35,050 --> 00:43:37,119
other than the victim
at Tateiwa's murder scene.

562
00:43:37,920 --> 00:43:38,987
What?

563
00:43:39,054 --> 00:43:42,057
There's no match in the police database.

564
00:43:42,691 --> 00:43:44,059
So, in other words…

565
00:43:47,696 --> 00:43:50,699
It's someone with no prior record…

566
00:44:10,285 --> 00:44:12,588
THE STABBING OF AN EXECUTIVE IN SHINAGAWA

567
00:44:13,288 --> 00:44:14,156
I knew it.

568
00:44:15,557 --> 00:44:17,760
It was your doing.

569
00:44:20,229 --> 00:44:23,799
It'd be troublesome for me if Mariko
gained any more power, wouldn't it?

570
00:44:26,869 --> 00:44:29,304
You really are incredible.

571
00:44:29,371 --> 00:44:30,739
My investigation was correct.

572
00:44:31,306 --> 00:44:33,976
I looked into you too, you know.

573
00:44:35,110 --> 00:44:38,213
Your background is very interesting.

574
00:44:39,848 --> 00:44:41,083
What are you

575
00:44:42,251 --> 00:44:43,752
to Mariko?

576
00:45:08,143 --> 00:45:09,077
Subtitle translation by:

